{"id": "EUVD-2026-102990", "enisaUuid": "79133db2-0172-3e8c-b920-e72608efc806", "description": "Niefy wx-api through 0.8.2 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to impersonate WeChat fans by supplying a raw openid cookie to fan-facing controllers. Attackers knowing a victim's openid can call /wxUser/getUserInfo and /wxUserTags endpoints to read nickname, phone, unionid and tags, and add or remove fan tags.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T21:13:48", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/wx-api-cross-tenant-idor-and-unauth-fan-pii", "https://github.com/niefy/wx-api/blob/0.8.2/src/main/java/com/github/niefy/modules/wx/controller/WxUserController.java#L31-L37", "https://github.com/niefy/wx-api/blob/0.8.2/src/main/java/com/github/niefy/modules/wx/controller/WxUserTagsController.java#L31-L45", "https://github.com/niefy/wx-api/blob/0.8.2/src/main/java/com/github/niefy/config/ShiroConfig.java#L43-L49", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/niefy-wx-api-through-0.8.2-authentication-bypass-via-unverified-openid-cookie"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111699", "GHSA-jqmh-3xm7-92j3"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "276a2df2-d1a8-33ee-8a0e-4d7e296e25fa", "product": {"name": "wx-api", "vendor": {"name": "niefy"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.8.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2160e22d-f7ea-3f6a-8ead-94383ae2c1ec", "vendor": {"name": "niefy"}}], "isExploited": false}